WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.836
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.270
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.639
between Nando's in the UK and the US.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.208
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.912
OK, slight problem.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.582
Nando's is in the US, but
it's only in four places:

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:18.618
Maryland, Illinois,
Virginia, and Washington, DC.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.153
Now, I'm in LA, baby.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.654
I'm on the wrong side of the Mississippi.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.123
But luckily I have a colleague

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:26.259
who is a Nando's enthusiast in Chicago.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:27.293
She frequented Nando's

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.928
when she was living in South Africa

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.331
and is perfect for taking the US reins

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.232
for this episode of "Food Wars."

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.635
Don't do "Food Wars"
without eating breakfast,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.436
I realize.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.605
Yeah, I've made that
mistake several times.

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:44.477
In the UK, Nando's chicken
comes in three serving sizes:

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.580
a quarter of a chicken...

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.314
Medha: In the US,

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.785
Nando's standard chicken
comes in just two sizes:

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.220
there's a half a chicken...

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.122
Harry: A whole chicken.

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.358
Medha: Or a fourth of a chicken.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.760
You can get a whole chicken in the US,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.395
but only as part of a platter.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.165
And we're going to weigh the whole chicken

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:08.401
to see which country's
chickens are bigger.

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.237
USA chicken, baby!

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.339
We can also get boneless thighs in the UK.

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.742
If you order these, they
come in a portion of four.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.378
Our thighs actually come
as a portion of three.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:20.280
So we got one, two, three.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.651
♪ Chicken, chicken wings ♪

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:25.919
♪ They're my favorite thing ♪

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.320
♪ And I love to sing ♪

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.321
If you haven't already seen it,

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.523
look up "The Nando's Skank,"

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.592
which is a very pure
distillation of British culture

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:34.160
in the late '00s.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.830
It's Ed Sheeran and Example rapping,

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.932
rapping about Nando's in a car park.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.100
I don't know why.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.235
And then he's just flexing his black card,

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:43.069
which I'm fuming about,

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.605
'cause, you know, Nando's black card,

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.041
they give them out to select individuals,

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.876
and it entitles you to free Nando's,

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.478
which I'm just so jealous of.

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.646
Also, bone to pick with that in general,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.615
why do they always give the
celebrities the free stuff?

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:56.749
Because they're the
people who need it least.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.650
They're already rich.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.718
Sort a guy out, come on.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.487
Cameraperson: But you are a celebrity now.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.788
I'm not a celebrity.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.256
Not yet.

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.291
Next up in the UK, we've got wings.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.526
They come in four portions:

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.761
portion of three.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:11.798
Medha: Our wings come as a serving of 12.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:13.099
Harry: A portion of five.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:16.002
Medha: Or a serving of 24.
Harry: A portion of 10.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.037
Or a portion of 15.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.140
If chicken on the bone isn't for you,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.141
Nando's also offers chicken

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.476
in the form of burgers, wraps, and pitas.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.845
In the UK, you can get these as singles

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.480
or as doubles.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:31.885
We can also get our chicken wrapped

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:34.320
or burgered.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.622
However, in the US,

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.758
there's no option to add double chicken,

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:40.026
which sucks.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:42.962
It's like a little burrito.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.999
Holy....

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:49.202
Don't do "Food Wars"
without eating breakfast.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.104
I'm going to cry.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:52.472
We're going to remove all the toppings

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.040
from the single chicken
burger and weigh it

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.508
to see how it compares to the US version.

00:02:55.742 --> 00:03:00.380
So, we're gonna take out
the tomato and the lettuce,

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.883
just like Harry mentioned.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.619
Which is good because tomato
does not belong on burgers

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.987
and never should.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.361
On the side of your chicken,

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.096
it's pretty common to get
some chips at Nando's.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.464
I'm excited for this episode,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.300
because I can actually
call them chips for once,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.935
as that's what they're
referred to on the US menu.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.036
Suck it, Joe.

00:03:23.036 --> 00:03:24.003
Medha: Suck it, Joe!

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.038
Joe: What did I do?
[all laugh]

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.706
Why is everyone telling me to suck it?

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.474
[laughing]

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.143
He's not even hosting this episode.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:32.378
I've just gotta send for him.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:32.612
[beep]

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:35.615
Chips in the UK come in
regular or large sizes.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:40.053
The standard US sizes
are regular and large.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.256
However, if you get them
as part of a platter,

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:47.327
you can get the bonus extra-large size.

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:50.964
Let's weigh the large fries
to see whose is bigger.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.565
Maybe I should have used the bowl.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.234
Oh, no.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.668
I'm still going to eat these.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:59.539
I don't care if they
touch all these gross....

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:00.406
Where is it?

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.175
OK.

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:07.347
I'm getting too good
at emptying brick chips

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:08.514
from containers.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.783
So, our scale is just about
adequate for this one,

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.585
and a portion of large fries in the UK –

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.187
I said fries. Why did I say fries?

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.189
I'm being conditioned to saying fries.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.190
That's right, buddy!

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.358
I heard you say fries!

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.626
This show is getting to me.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:19.759
[beep]

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:22.996
A portion of large chips in the
UK comes to about 498 grams.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:25.365
Medha: 150 grams.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.333
What about the biggest thing
on each country's menu?

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.502
Well, in the UK, it's
this: the family platter.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.937
It comes with two whole chickens,

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.071
five large sides,

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.307
and will cost you 43 pounds and 70 pence.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:38.978
The biggest US item is the jumbo platter.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.948
It includes two whole chickens

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.517
with two extra-large sides

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.986
for $52.99.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.058
Let's take a look at some
of the nutritional standouts

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:53.159
from the Nando's menu.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:54.294
If you were to get a standard meal,

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.461
it might look something like this:

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.997
half a chicken, a portion
of peri-salted chips,

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.232
and a portion of Macho peas.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:02.568
In the UK, this will come to
a total of 1,228 calories,

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.137
which honestly isn't too bad.

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:06.005
There's also nothing
really alarming on that.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:07.573
The only notable thing is that it contains

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:10.677
186.4% of your daily protein intake.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:15.481
Over here it comes out to 1,124 calories,

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:19.118
which is actually a little
less than the UK's version.

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:22.322
Our chicken and chips are
actually a little less calorific

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:24.891
than the UK's, but for some reason,

00:05:24.891 --> 00:05:27.493
our Macho peas are more calorific.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.062
What's the sitch?

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:34.867
Already I can tell
there's a bunch of spices

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:37.270
and seasoning on the peas.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.972
I'm thinking butter is involved.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.442
Ugh, I hate peas.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:45.178
That is not what I was expecting.

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.713
It does have a kick to it.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:47.780
Based on the ingredients,

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.749
there's not really anything alarming

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:52.352
that we see in the US version either.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.786
There's just a lot of sodium in it,

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:56.289
which is kind of expected
because of all the spices

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:58.257
and the seasoning that goes into it.

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.459
One thing to watch out for

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:01.894
is the basting flavor of your chicken.

00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:05.765
Somehow, if you get your
chicken as extra hot in the US,

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:10.370
it adds 4,611 milligrams of sodium.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.672
That's double your daily allowance,

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.340
just for the baste.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.742
Joe: That's so much sodium.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:16.976
Medha: That's insane.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.145
What about the most calorific
thing on the UK menu?

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:20.380
Well, it might not surprise you to learn

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.848
that it's actually a whole chicken.

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:24.217
Extra hot is also the least
healthy baste in the UK,

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.718
with an extra-hot whole chicken coming in

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:28.187
at 1,299 calories.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:30.423
However, a whole chicken actually isn't

00:06:30.423 --> 00:06:33.025
the most calorific thing
on the menu in the US.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:35.361
This is the Nandoca's Choice burger,

00:06:35.361 --> 00:06:37.530
which is a butterflied chicken breast

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.833
and coleslaw in between garlic-bread buns.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.736
Dude, a burger with
garlic bread for a bun?

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.204
That sounds so good.

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:47.507
That is a genius idea. Send me that.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.711
One of these comes at 1,003 calories.

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:53.346
It looks like the main culprit here

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:55.181
is the garlic-bread buns.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:56.482
On the US menu,

00:06:56.482 --> 00:07:00.987
the garlic bread is the
most calorific regular side,

00:07:00.987 --> 00:07:04.891
and it's the highest-cholesterol
side as well.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:07.193
Kinda wanna try it.

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:12.565
It's not what you would expect.

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:14.700
It's not like US garlic bread.

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:15.868
That's a little strange,

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.203
as the UK's most calorific side

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:19.005
is actually the peri-salted chips.

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.873
These come in at 519 calories,

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:23.409
whereas the garlic bread is only 362.

00:07:23.409 --> 00:07:25.144
What are you guys doing
to your garlic bread?

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:28.714
I think we're just making
our garlic bread tastier.

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:32.552
It feels like you're
trying to attack me, Harry.

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:33.753
Trying to attack the US.

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:35.621
We don't like that.

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:39.759
While the garlic bread may
be high in cholesterol,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:43.529
it pales in comparison
to one item in that area,

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.798
which is the chicken livers.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.533
One serving of these

00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:51.571
contain 978 milligrams of cholesterol,

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:54.073
comfortably the highest thing on the menu.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:57.510
More than triple your
daily recommended amount.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.512
UK Nando's don't disclose
cholesterol content,

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:00.947
but they do disclose fat content.

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:02.748
The fattiest thing on
the menu is, once again,

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:03.749
the whole chicken.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.519
One of these contains 54.4 grams of fat,

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.788
which is around 69% of
your daily allowance.

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:10.690
[whispering] Nice. Nice.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.425
Medha: [whispering] I wanna try that too.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.259
Harry: Nice.

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:14.360
Nice.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.695
Nice.

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:16.262
OK.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:20.266
Unfortunately, Nando's doesn't disclose

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.701
the full ingredients list in the UK.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:24.337
Same here. All we get are allergens,

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:25.638
and the allergen list

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:27.940
doesn't contain anything too alarming.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.108
We reached out to Nando's

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:31.344
for more information
about the ingredients.

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:33.946
They told us that all their chicken meets

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:37.850
or exceeds USDA quality
standards and is never frozen.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.386
They also grow their own
African bird's eye chilies

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:42.154
on farms across South Africa

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.724
for an authentic peri-peri spice.

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:46.125
One piece of information you can get

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:47.527
from the UK's FAQ page

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.996
is that the plant-based
Great Imitator wrap

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:52.064
might not actually be as
plant-based as it seems.

00:08:52.064 --> 00:08:55.134
The baste and the tortilla
wrap used both contain shellac.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:57.370
Now, shellac is also sometimes
called confectioner's glaze,

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.437
and it's a natural polymer

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:00.640
that's used to give things a waxy finish

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.074
and to trap in moisture,

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:03.809
but where does shellac actually come from?

00:09:03.809 --> 00:09:06.345
Well, it's actually secreted
by female lac beetles

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:08.648
onto trees in India and Thailand.

00:09:08.681 --> 00:09:10.316
This means it's technically
an animal product,

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:12.618
and although it can be gathered
without harming the beetles,

00:09:12.618 --> 00:09:14.186
this is hard to achieve in practice.

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:15.187
Not nice.

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:18.224
It's worth pointing out one
other FAQ from the UK page,

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:20.593
which is that the UK Nando's
have explicitly committed

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:23.429
to never using chlorinated
chicken from America.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.364
Chlorinated chicken's been in
the headlines a lot recently

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:26.766
because it's kind of become the face

00:09:26.766 --> 00:09:29.368
of differing food standards
between the UK and the US.

00:09:29.402 --> 00:09:31.304
It refers to the process of
giving slaughtered chickens

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:32.939
a chemical wash before they're packaged

00:09:32.939 --> 00:09:34.140
and sent to consumers.

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:37.610
What do you guys have against
our chlorinated chicken?

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.378
JK. Joking. You're gonna see.

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:41.147
There's so many things against
our chlorinated chicken.

00:09:41.514 --> 00:09:44.383
This is done to kill harmful
bacteria like salmonella.

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:46.185
Even the European Union admits

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:49.388
that it's unlikely to pose
any health risk to consumers.

00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:52.458
But campaigners say that
it also allows farmers

00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:54.393
to cover up lower production standards

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:56.228
throughout the chicken-rearing process.

00:09:56.228 --> 00:09:58.364
The good news is that it's estimated

00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:00.466
only 10% of US chicken

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:02.735
actually gets treated with chlorine.

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:05.905
So it's not a guarantee that
Nando's chicken in the US

00:10:05.905 --> 00:10:07.607
will have been through the process,

00:10:07.607 --> 00:10:09.842
but it's an interesting example

00:10:09.842 --> 00:10:13.646
of the different food
standards in the UK and the US.

00:10:13.946 --> 00:10:15.881
Chicken tastes pretty good over here, so,

00:10:15.881 --> 00:10:16.816
it is what it is.

00:10:19.552 --> 00:10:20.720
Here is everything you will only find

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.954
on the menu at a UK Nando's.

00:10:22.254 --> 00:10:25.257
And here's everything you can only find

00:10:25.257 --> 00:10:27.460
on the menu at a US Nando's.

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:29.061
Let's start with some chicken options.

00:10:29.462 --> 00:10:31.497
Here we got the Sunset
Burger, which is currently,

00:10:31.497 --> 00:10:33.699
I believe, exclusive
to delivery platforms.

00:10:33.699 --> 00:10:35.301
This is a soft roll.

00:10:35.301 --> 00:10:37.103
And then it also contains chicken thighs,

00:10:37.103 --> 00:10:39.972
cheddar cheese, red pepper
chutney, mayo, and lettuce.

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:41.607
Next up, we've got Chicken Wing Roulette.

00:10:41.607 --> 00:10:42.441
Now, what this is,

00:10:42.441 --> 00:10:44.777
is 10 chicken wings of
varying spice levels.

00:10:44.777 --> 00:10:46.045
The idea, I guess, is that you order

00:10:46.045 --> 00:10:47.913
a plate of these for
yourself and your friends,

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:48.781
you all pick one or two,

00:10:48.781 --> 00:10:51.317
and the loser gets blasted
with some extra-hot sauce.

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:53.152
Now, obviously we have
to try this ourselves.

00:10:53.152 --> 00:10:55.721
So myself and our cameraperson, Laura,

00:10:55.721 --> 00:10:57.390
are going to give this
a go and see who loses.

00:10:57.556 --> 00:10:58.424
Laura: Are we doing this now?

00:10:58.424 --> 00:11:00.092
Harry: I think we are.
Laura: All right.

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:00.960
OK that one looks...

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:02.461
yeah, you're going dangerous, aren't you?

00:11:02.461 --> 00:11:04.296
Harry: I'm going for,
like, a menacingly red one.

00:11:04.296 --> 00:11:05.464
Laura: Yes, you are. I'm going for

00:11:05.464 --> 00:11:06.799
the less menacing-looking one.

00:11:06.799 --> 00:11:07.667
Harry: Well, hopefully it's a red herring

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:08.934
and I've done this to deceive you.

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:10.069
Harry: Cheers.
Laura: Cheers.

00:11:13.272 --> 00:11:14.440
Laura: Absolutely fine.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:15.374
Harry: It was OK?
Laura: Yeah.

00:11:15.374 --> 00:11:17.643
It is spicy. It's not,
like, blowing my head off.

00:11:17.643 --> 00:11:19.812
I feel like mine's maybe hot?

00:11:19.812 --> 00:11:20.680
But if that's extra hot,

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:21.814
then I'm, like, very underwhelmed.

00:11:21.981 --> 00:11:22.915
Slight anticlimax.

00:11:22.915 --> 00:11:24.617
I think Laura maybe
just got, like, a medium

00:11:24.617 --> 00:11:26.619
or a plain one, because
she was not fazed at all.

00:11:26.619 --> 00:11:28.354
I think maybe I got hot?

00:11:28.354 --> 00:11:29.188
If that was extra hot,

00:11:29.188 --> 00:11:30.356
I'm very disappointed. All I'll say.

00:11:30.556 --> 00:11:31.824
Little cocky there, buddy.

00:11:32.024 --> 00:11:33.192
So, I got myself a bottle

00:11:33.192 --> 00:11:36.429
of the Nando's Peri-Peri XX hot sauce,

00:11:36.429 --> 00:11:39.932
and I too want to try the
spiciest level that they offer.

00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:42.001
OK. Whoop, that might've been too much.

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.371
That's extra hot, huh?

00:11:45.371 --> 00:11:46.939
No, not very strong.

00:11:46.939 --> 00:11:49.108
I like the flavor a
lot on it, but – wait.

00:11:50.276 --> 00:11:51.510
Hm, definitely manageable.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.412
Yeah. I mean, like, I love
the flavor of all this stuff.

00:11:53.412 --> 00:11:54.714
It's just not that hot.

00:11:55.815 --> 00:11:56.816
[sneezes]

00:11:57.316 --> 00:11:58.984
Now, for those of you who
think I got off lightly

00:11:58.984 --> 00:12:00.386
and actually want to see me in pain,

00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:02.221
you're in luck, because in the UK

00:12:02.221 --> 00:12:03.622
we have an exclusive spice level

00:12:03.622 --> 00:12:05.191
that goes above extra hot.

00:12:05.191 --> 00:12:08.794
Here we have three chicken
wings coated in Vusa XX sauce,

00:12:08.794 --> 00:12:10.496
which is one level above extra hot

00:12:10.496 --> 00:12:12.131
on the Nando's Peri-ometer.

00:12:12.131 --> 00:12:13.232
These already look hotter

00:12:13.232 --> 00:12:14.500
than anything that was
in the roulette box.

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.336
There's lots of chili flakes
on them that are visible,

00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:19.338
and it's just that kind of,
like, alarming red color

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:20.539
that if you see a snake that color,

00:12:20.539 --> 00:12:22.174
you're supposed to run away from.

00:12:22.374 --> 00:12:24.376
Cameraperson: Don't you just run
away from snakes in general?

00:12:24.643 --> 00:12:26.545
Some snakes are friendly. [laughs]

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.114
Grass snakes. Grass snakes are cool.

00:12:28.114 --> 00:12:29.648
And, of course, because I hate myself,

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:31.117
I'm going to try one of these.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.585
They didn't give us gloves,

00:12:32.585 --> 00:12:34.420
like they did in the Wingstop episode,

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:36.388
which I guess is a good sign?

00:12:36.555 --> 00:12:39.091
I'm not great with spice,
so let's see how this goes.

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:45.264
Hm.

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:46.365
Bit of a slow burn.

00:12:47.299 --> 00:12:48.701
Really slow burn.

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:50.603
Not really getting much
from this, I'll be honest.

00:12:50.603 --> 00:12:52.204
Maybe if I just rub my eyes.

00:12:52.338 --> 00:12:53.305
I'm not really getting it.

00:12:53.305 --> 00:12:54.240
That's disappointing.

00:12:54.740 --> 00:12:56.342
I, like I say, I'm not good with spice.

00:12:57.409 --> 00:12:59.044
But I'm handling that with ease.

00:12:59.044 --> 00:12:59.845
Nando's, come on.

00:12:59.945 --> 00:13:01.080
It would have made for better content

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:02.948
if you made me cry, guys, so.

00:13:02.948 --> 00:13:04.350
It's about the same as
what I got from there.

00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:07.520
Y'all tried your really hot wings, right?

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:11.624
Well, I just wanted a
taste of the hot sauce

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:13.159
that they provided us with here.

00:13:13.159 --> 00:13:16.595
If I can get it open at
any point in my life.

00:13:18.964 --> 00:13:19.398
Hulk.

00:13:19.498 --> 00:13:22.935
Nando's peri-peri sauce, hot. Gluten-free.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:27.473
[coughs]

00:13:27.473 --> 00:13:28.307
Excuse me.

00:13:31.377 --> 00:13:32.878
[coughs]

00:13:32.878 --> 00:13:35.514
Committing su–[laughs and coughs]

00:13:35.514 --> 00:13:36.415
Cameraperson: Was it that hot?

00:13:36.549 --> 00:13:37.449
No.

00:13:37.516 --> 00:13:38.651
That's for the camera.

00:13:38.651 --> 00:13:39.351
Cameraperson: What?!

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:41.420
[laughing]

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:44.356
I should get an Oscar.

00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:46.759
[crowd cheers]

00:13:46.759 --> 00:13:47.693
It was a little hot.

00:13:47.693 --> 00:13:48.494
Cameraperson: OK.

00:13:48.527 --> 00:13:50.196
But it wasn't, like,
too hot, like I'm dying.

00:13:50.196 --> 00:13:51.230
Cameraperson: It's kinda spicy,

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.364
but this already has...

00:13:52.498 --> 00:13:53.866
I did that to trick you.

00:13:53.866 --> 00:13:55.701
Do you see how I became a double agent?

00:13:55.701 --> 00:13:56.335
Cameraperson: Wow.

00:13:56.902 --> 00:13:57.870
I actually did have a reaction.

00:13:57.870 --> 00:13:58.571
Cameraperson: It's good though.

00:13:58.571 --> 00:13:59.438
It's really sweet.

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:01.073
It just hits you in the throat.

00:14:01.073 --> 00:14:01.907
It's like...[whacks throat]

00:14:02.374 --> 00:14:03.843
Now, at the other end of
the heat scale from Vusa,

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:05.177
we have one more exclusive baste,

00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:06.579
which is the Peri-Tamer.

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:08.380
This is described as mild and sweet,

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:10.149
and it's just for people
who don't really like spice.

00:14:10.149 --> 00:14:10.983
And then finally we have something

00:14:10.983 --> 00:14:12.251
that isn't technically chicken,

00:14:12.251 --> 00:14:14.620
but more of a chicken replacement.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.655
This is the Great Imitator wrap.

00:14:16.655 --> 00:14:19.058
It contains imitation chicken
made from pea protein.

00:14:19.158 --> 00:14:23.729
So, we have some exclusive
chicken items of our own, Harry.

00:14:23.729 --> 00:14:26.332
We can get these chicken thigh skewers,

00:14:26.332 --> 00:14:29.535
which come with red pepper and onions,

00:14:29.535 --> 00:14:32.438
and they look salivating.

00:14:32.738 --> 00:14:35.074
We can also get these chicken livers,

00:14:35.074 --> 00:14:38.444
which you won't currently
find on the UK menu

00:14:38.444 --> 00:14:39.545
due to the pandemic.

00:14:39.545 --> 00:14:41.614
The Thigh and Mighty sandwich.

00:14:41.614 --> 00:14:45.084
Then we can get a chicken
Caesar in the form of a wrap

00:14:45.084 --> 00:14:46.552
or a pita bread.

00:14:46.585 --> 00:14:48.687
Also got a lot of salad bowls,

00:14:48.754 --> 00:14:51.423
and that you won't find in the UK.

00:14:51.423 --> 00:14:54.093
There's a peri-peri chicken tender bowl,

00:14:54.093 --> 00:14:56.996
an ancient grains bowl,

00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:58.797
a chicken Caesar salad,

00:14:58.797 --> 00:15:01.267
a tomato and Halloumi salad,

00:15:01.267 --> 00:15:05.304
and chicken and avocado
and pepper roasted bowl,

00:15:05.304 --> 00:15:10.309
and a cauliflower, butternut,
and Halloumi salad.

00:15:10.843 --> 00:15:12.111
It's just, like, a lot of salad.

00:15:12.111 --> 00:15:13.913
That's not my cup of tea.

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:15.347
This is my cup of tea.

00:15:15.948 --> 00:15:18.217
We have two exclusive
appetizers in the UK.

00:15:18.217 --> 00:15:22.321
Firstly, we have Halloumi
sticks with a chili jam dip,

00:15:22.321 --> 00:15:24.423
and then we have some sweet potato wedges,

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:26.725
which are served with a garlic Perinaise.

00:15:26.725 --> 00:15:28.494
I do not like sweet potato.

00:15:28.494 --> 00:15:30.095
I wish people would stop
serving it on menus.

00:15:30.095 --> 00:15:32.331
It is always worse than
chips and always costs more.

00:15:32.898 --> 00:15:35.668
So, we only get the one
exclusive appetizer:

00:15:35.668 --> 00:15:36.669
the garlic sticks.

00:15:36.936 --> 00:15:38.037
On the side of your meal in the UK,

00:15:38.037 --> 00:15:39.305
we have a few exclusive sides,

00:15:39.305 --> 00:15:41.941
such as corn on the cob,

00:15:41.941 --> 00:15:43.776
some long-stem broccoli,

00:15:43.776 --> 00:15:47.112
spicy rice, and finally
we have some coleslaw.

00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:50.382
Our exclusive sides are
a Caesar side salad,

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:53.018
Portuguese rice, winter roasted veggies,

00:15:53.018 --> 00:15:57.156
butternut squash, and corn,
and braised brussels sprouts.

00:15:57.423 --> 00:15:58.891
Now, in addition to the Vusa sauce,

00:15:58.891 --> 00:16:01.026
we also have garlic
Perinaise, as I mentioned,

00:16:01.026 --> 00:16:02.428
which comes with the sweet potato wedges,

00:16:02.861 --> 00:16:05.297
and we have this one, which
is a peri barbecue sauce.

00:16:05.464 --> 00:16:07.499
The only exclusive sauce we have

00:16:07.499 --> 00:16:09.969
is a coconut lemon peri-peri sauce.

00:16:10.235 --> 00:16:11.170
It would take a while to go through

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.204
all of the exclusive drinks,

00:16:12.204 --> 00:16:13.505
so we're just going to
show you some highlights,

00:16:13.505 --> 00:16:14.506
such as this.

00:16:14.506 --> 00:16:17.443
This is a Gingerella, which
is an organic ginger ale.

00:16:17.576 --> 00:16:20.479
Nix &amp; Kix sparkling cucumber-mint drink

00:16:20.479 --> 00:16:21.680
with a hint of cayenne.

00:16:21.847 --> 00:16:23.682
And, of course, we have this one,

00:16:23.682 --> 00:16:25.617
which is a Royal Flush kombucha.

00:16:25.617 --> 00:16:26.819
Now, I personally like kombucha.

00:16:26.819 --> 00:16:29.154
I know it's a little bit
divisive, but it's pretty good.

00:16:29.355 --> 00:16:31.190
We can also get alcohol from a UK Nando's.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.726
We've got some lager,
some pilsner, an IPA,

00:16:33.726 --> 00:16:34.660
and a white wine.

00:16:34.994 --> 00:16:38.897
La Croix, and Bundaberg ginger beer,

00:16:39.298 --> 00:16:41.200
this Honest iced tea,

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.669
as well as a Mexican Coke,

00:16:43.669 --> 00:16:46.638
which, throw me the bottle opener!

00:16:46.739 --> 00:16:48.941
We also got alcohol too.

00:16:48.941 --> 00:16:50.676
We got beer and wine.

00:16:50.676 --> 00:16:54.480
We can get rose sangria
and spiked lemonade.

00:16:57.983 --> 00:16:58.517
Nice.

00:16:58.517 --> 00:17:01.053
And our only exclusive dessert option

00:17:01.053 --> 00:17:03.022
is this Barely Baked brownie.

00:17:03.622 --> 00:17:05.124
Let's finish out with the desserts.

00:17:05.124 --> 00:17:06.625
In the UK, you can close out your meal

00:17:06.625 --> 00:17:09.895
with a slice of Choc-A-Lot
cake, which is really good.

00:17:09.895 --> 00:17:10.929
It's very moist.

00:17:10.963 --> 00:17:13.699
With a slice of white chocolate
and raspberry cheesecake,

00:17:13.699 --> 00:17:16.635
and finally a gooey caramel cheesecake.

00:17:16.702 --> 00:17:17.836
I thought I'd have a crack at explaining

00:17:17.836 --> 00:17:19.338
the whole "cheeky Nando's" phenomenon

00:17:19.338 --> 00:17:20.906
to our viewers from across the pond.

00:17:20.906 --> 00:17:22.975
If you were on the internet,
like, five or 10 years ago,

00:17:22.975 --> 00:17:24.410
you've probably seen this phrase.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.078
It just kind of refers to this time

00:17:26.078 --> 00:17:28.047
where cheeky Nando's with the lads

00:17:28.047 --> 00:17:29.648
was just the go-to activity.

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:31.850
It was like, mostly teenage
boys would go into town

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:33.685
for a day out, wander around the shops,

00:17:33.685 --> 00:17:35.287
end up in Nando's, have a meal,

00:17:35.287 --> 00:17:37.189
and then usually Instagram or Snapchat it

00:17:37.189 --> 00:17:39.191
with the caption "cheeky
Nando's with the lads"

00:17:39.191 --> 00:17:40.225
with this emoji.

00:17:41.126 --> 00:17:44.296
I'm going to make that my
next Instagram caption.

00:17:44.296 --> 00:17:46.532
Cheeky Nando's with the lads.

00:17:46.532 --> 00:17:48.133
Clancy's my lad.

00:17:48.133 --> 00:17:50.235
Come here, Clancy.

00:17:50.235 --> 00:17:51.937
[laughs]

00:17:51.937 --> 00:17:54.373
Cheeky Nando's with the lads!

00:17:54.373 --> 00:17:55.507
["The Nando's Skank" plays]

00:17:55.507 --> 00:17:57.142
Medha: Harry, you gotta bust a move more.

00:17:57.142 --> 00:17:58.610
["The Nando's Skank" plays]

00:17:58.610 --> 00:18:00.345
♪ Chicken ♪

00:18:00.646 --> 00:18:03.782
Joe: Yeah, no thanks on
that, guys. Uh, no, thanks.

00:18:03.782 --> 00:18:05.350
♪ And I love to sing ♪

00:18:05.951 --> 00:18:06.885
That's quite enough of that.

00:18:06.885 --> 00:18:08.120
[laughs]

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:09.922
♪ Chicken wings ♪

00:18:09.922 --> 00:18:11.256
♪ They're my favorite thing ♪

00:18:11.256 --> 00:18:13.158
♪ And I love to sing ♪

00:18:13.792 --> 00:18:15.561
All right! Another "Food Wars" episode

00:18:15.561 --> 00:18:18.063
where I did almost nothing.

00:18:18.297 --> 00:18:20.065
I could get used to this.

00:18:20.065 --> 00:18:22.067
[groans]

